<div class="min-h-screen bg-[#f4f1e9] text-slate-950">
  <header id="kialo-comparison-hero" class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-white">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-14 sm:px-8 sm:py-20">
      <p class="border-l-2 border-teal-700 pl-3 text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">
        Free Kialo alternative
      </p>
      <h1 class="mt-5 max-w-4xl font-serif text-5xl font-semibold leading-[1.02] tracking-tight sm:text-7xl">
        A free Kialo alternative for exploring arguments.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-5 text-lg leading-8 text-slate-600">
        If you are looking for a Kialo alternative, first decide whether you need a debate platform or a broader inquiry map.
        <a
          href="https://www.kialo.com/"
          target="_blank"
          rel="noopener noreferrer"
          class="font-semibold text-teal-800 underline decoration-teal-600 underline-offset-4"
        >Kialo</a>
        centres structured pro and con discussion and is especially visible in education. RationalGrid is a free, not-for-profit, AI-assisted space for branching from questions into answers, challenges, evidence, sources, and notes.
      </p>
      <div class="mt-8 flex flex-wrap gap-3">
        <a
          id="kialo-start-cta"
          href="/?focus=grid#start-here"
          data-analytics-event="comparison_start_grid_clicked"
          data-analytics-comparison="kialo"
          data-analytics-placement="hero"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-slate-950 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-white hover:bg-slate-800"
        >Start a grid <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></a><a
          id="kialo-guide-link"
          href="/intro/how"
          class="inline-flex items-center gap-2 border-b border-slate-500 px-1 py-2 text-sm font-semibold hover:border-teal-700 hover:text-teal-800"
        >See how grids work <.icon name="hero-arrow-up-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </header>

  <main class="mx-auto max-w-6xl px-5 py-12 sm:px-8 sm:py-16">
    <section id="kialo-verdict" aria-labelledby="kialo-verdict-heading">
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">Short verdict</p><h2
        id="kialo-verdict-heading"
        class="mt-2 font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight"
      >
        Choose around the shape of the activity.
      </h2><p class="mt-4 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Kialo is a natural fit when participants are organising reasons for and against a thesis. RationalGrid fits exploratory work where the next move may be a new question, an AI-assisted answer, a challenge, a source, a note, or a separate branch—not only a pro or con.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="kialo-at-a-glance" class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="kialo-table-heading">
      <h2 id="kialo-table-heading" class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        At a glance
      </h2><div class="mt-6 overflow-x-auto border border-stone-300 bg-white">
        <table id="kialo-comparison-table" class="w-full min-w-[44rem] border-collapse text-left">
          <thead>
            <tr class="border-b border-stone-300 bg-stone-100">
              <th class="px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold">Dimension</th><th class="px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold">
                Kialo
              </th><th class="bg-teal-950 px-5 py-4 text-sm font-semibold text-white">
                RationalGrid
              </th>
            </tr>
          </thead><tbody class="divide-y divide-stone-300 text-sm leading-6">
            <%= for {dimension, kialo, grid} <- [
        {"Core shape", "Claims arranged around supporting and opposing reasons.", "Typed branches including questions, answers, challenges, evidence, sources, and notes."},
        {"Starting point", "A thesis or discussion proposition.", "A question, topic, or idea to explore."},
        {"AI role", "Check Kialo's current product information for its available features.", "AI can suggest answers and branches; people choose, assess, and edit the path."},
        {"Good fit", "Deliberation, debate preparation, and structured classroom discussion.", "Open-ended inquiry, topic exploration, and a durable map of connected thinking."},
        {"Cost and purpose", "Consult Kialo for current plans and terms.", "Free to use and run on a not-for-profit basis."}
      ] do %>
              <tr>
                <th scope="row" class="bg-[#f8f6f0] px-5 py-4 font-semibold">{dimension}</th><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-600">
                  {kialo}
                </td><td class="px-5 py-4 text-slate-700">{grid}</td>
              </tr>
            <% end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="kialo-strengths"
      class="mt-14 grid gap-5 md:grid-cols-2"
      aria-label="What each option does well"
    >
      <article class="border-t-4 border-sky-600 bg-white p-6">
        <.icon name="hero-scale" class="h-6 w-6 text-sky-700" /><h2 class="mt-4 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">
          What Kialo does well
        </h2><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
          Its pro/con structure makes the relationship between a claim and the reasons supporting or opposing it legible. That focus can help a class or group examine a contested proposition without losing the debate’s outline.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article class="border-t-4 border-teal-700 bg-slate-950 p-6 text-white">
        <.icon name="hero-sparkles" class="h-6 w-6 text-teal-300" /><h2 class="mt-4 font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">
          What RationalGrid does well
        </h2><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-300">
          It supports more kinds of move within one map. Ask AI for a starting answer, challenge a precise point, request evidence, add your own note, preserve a source, or open a different question while the origin remains visible.
        </p>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section
      id="kialo-choose"
      class="mt-14 border-y border-stone-300 py-10"
      aria-labelledby="kialo-choose-heading"
    >
      <h2 id="kialo-choose-heading" class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold tracking-tight">
        Choose each if…
      </h2><div class="mt-7 grid gap-6 md:grid-cols-2">
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Choose Kialo if…</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-slate-600">
            <li>• The activity is explicitly a pro/con discussion.</li><li>
              • Participants need a shared view of reasons around a thesis.
            </li><li>
              • You want a debate-focused format, particularly for teaching or deliberation.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h3 class="text-lg font-semibold">Choose RationalGrid if…</h3><ul class="mt-3 space-y-3 text-slate-600">
            <li>• You are discovering the questions as you go.</li><li>
              • AI assistance can help open paths, while human judgement stays central.
            </li><li>• Different branch types, notes, sources, and later revisiting matter.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section
      id="kialo-caveat"
      class="mt-12 border border-stone-300 border-l-4 border-l-amber-600 bg-white p-6"
    >
      <h2 class="font-serif text-3xl font-semibold">
        Do not mistake a tidy tree for a settled issue.
      </h2><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
        Either interface can make an argument look clearer than its evidence warrants. Categories overlap, people disagree about framing, and a missing reason may matter more than the visible ones. Treat the structure as a prompt for judgement, not a scorecard.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section id="kialo-faq" class="mt-14" aria-labelledby="kialo-faq-heading">
      <h2 id="kialo-faq-heading" class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold">FAQ</h2><div class="mt-6 divide-y divide-stone-300 border-y border-stone-300">
        <%= for {question, answer} <- [
        {"Can I import a Kialo discussion directly into RationalGrid?", "No. RationalGrid does not currently provide a direct Kialo import. You would need to recreate or selectively transfer the material, subject to any applicable permissions."},
        {"Is RationalGrid a formal logic tool?", "No. Its typed branches clarify the role an item plays, but they do not turn an inquiry into a formal proof or certify that an argument is valid."},
        {"Is RationalGrid free?", "Yes. RationalGrid is free to use and is run on a not-for-profit basis."},
        {"Which is better for a classroom debate?", "Kialo's focused pro/con format may be the clearer choice for a defined debate. RationalGrid may suit a class that needs to generate questions, explore context, and retain sources as well as compare objections."}
      ] do %>
          <details class="py-5">
            <summary class="cursor-pointer font-semibold">{question}</summary><p class="mt-3 leading-7 text-slate-600">
              {answer}
            </p>
          </details>
        <% end %>
      </div>
    </section>

    <nav
      id="kialo-related-comparisons"
      class="mt-14 border-t border-stone-300 pt-8"
      aria-label="Related comparisons"
    >
      <p class="text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-teal-800">Keep comparing</p>
      <div class="mt-4 flex flex-wrap gap-x-6 gap-y-3 text-sm font-semibold">
        <a
          href="/compare/chatgpt"
          class="text-teal-800 underline decoration-stone-400 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-teal-700"
        >ChatGPT alternatives for structured research</a>
        <a
          href="/compare/mind-maps"
          class="text-teal-800 underline decoration-stone-400 underline-offset-4 hover:decoration-teal-700"
        >Argument maps vs mind maps</a>
      </div>
    </nav>

    <section id="kialo-final-cta" class="mt-14 bg-teal-950 p-7 text-white sm:p-10">
      <h2 class="font-serif text-4xl font-semibold">
        Start with curiosity, then give disagreement a place.
      </h2><p class="mt-3 text-teal-100">
        Build a free grid and follow the questions, challenges, and evidence that emerge.
      </p><a
        id="kialo-final-cta-link"
        href="/?focus=grid#start-here"
        data-analytics-event="comparison_start_grid_clicked"
        data-analytics-comparison="kialo"
        data-analytics-placement="final_cta"
        class="mt-6 inline-flex items-center gap-2 rounded-md bg-teal-300 px-5 py-3 text-sm font-semibold text-slate-950 hover:bg-teal-200"
      >Start a free grid <.icon name="hero-arrow-right" class="h-4 w-4" /></a>
    </section>
  </main>
</div>
